From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 05:06:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 001/220] [ae-patch] Show the ae.status label on session rows
 and a Slots n/3 pill in the sidebar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 2 of omnigent-ae (patch P1, 2026-09-23). Status is a label, never a
title glyph: each session row now prefixes a lucide icon for its `ae.status`
(working CirclePlay, blocked CirclePause, review CircleCheck, parked
CircleParking, reference Archive), and the primary navigation carries a
"Slots n/3" pill that counts the working, top-level, unarchived rows in the
`["conversations"]` query cache and turns red at three. Blocked is derived: a
working session with an approval prompt outstanding shows the blocked icon.
A leading legacy title glyph (🟡 🔴 ✅ 📌 🗂️) is stripped for display only;
nothing writes a glyph back and the rename seed keeps the stored title.

Logic lives in new files (web/src/lib/aeLabels.ts mirrors the AE layer's
labels.py; AeStatusIcon.tsx; AeSlotsPill.tsx) so the upstream edits stay
small: four lines in Sidebar.tsx, two in sidebarNav.ts, four in
ExtensionPrimaryNavigation.tsx (the circle-parking and gauge icon names the
Parking Lot extension will use). Tests cover the helpers, both components and
the sidebar rows through the row-actions scaffold.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
